# API & Data Layer

## Services

- One domain folder under `services/` (e.g. `Cell/cell.service.ts` + `cell.types.ts`)
- All HTTP calls go through `secureFetch` from `@/utils/secureFetch`
- Use `apiEndpoints` from `@/utils/endpoints` — add new routes there first
- Backend responses use `ReturnVal`: `{ success, message?, data?, status_code? }`

```typescript
// ✅ Service pattern
export const fetchCells = async (): Promise<Cell[]> => {
  const response = await secureFetch(apiEndpoints.cells.getAll);
  const json: ReturnVal = await response.json();
  return json.data as Cell[];
};
```

- Throw `{ status, message }` on failure when hooks need retry logic
- Guest/unauthenticated calls: `secureFetch(url, init, { allowUnauthenticated: true })`

## React Query Hooks

- Place in `hooks/<Domain>/useXxxQuery.ts` or `useXxxMutation.ts`
- Name hooks `useCellsQuery`, `usePeopleFlowMutation` (domain + action)
- Use stable `queryKey` arrays: `["cells"]`, `["people", id]`
- Do not retry on 401/403 (match existing hooks)
- Screens consume hooks — do not call services directly from `app/` routes
